# Text files are LF in the repository and in every checkout, Windows included.
# rustfmt, snapshots and byte-exact tests then agree on both OSes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures are stored and checked out exactly as they were recorded: CRLF,
# mixed line endings and byte-order marks are what some of them test.
**/fixtures/** -text

# Binary assets.
*.png binary

# Scripts that only run on Windows keep the line endings Windows tools expect.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# The open items' index is written by `cargo xtask outstanding` from the items'
# files. Merged line by line, keeping both sides, so that a rebase never stops
# on it; `cargo xtask rules` finds what such a merge gets wrong, and the command
# puts it right.
docs/outstanding/README.md merge=union
